      "contracts": [
        "RendererInputProps is exactly {question, disabled, inputId, labelId, valueIndex?} — inputs take no value/onChange; they self-subscribe via useQuestionResponse(question.id). Any new renderer that wants to reuse inputs verbatim must expose the SAME module-level jotai atoms (store.ts's responsesAtom) through its own Provider — Jotai scopes atoms per Provider store, so a new provider instance reusing these atom objects works without touching the input files.",
        "useQuestionResponse's setter is a silent no-op when responsesAtom has no entry for that question id (`if (!current) return`). Any live tree update that adds a question MUST add its response entry, or the new input renders but cannot be typed into. NoteAffordance and StructuredQuestionSlot additionally render null when the entry is missing.",
        "initializeResponses only creates entries for non-group questions, keyed by question.id, seeding answer_option.initial_selected as {type:'string', value, coding}. Re-seeding with it wholesale (current RendererContext behavior) destroys all in-progress answers — live builder updates need a merge that keeps existing entries by id and only adds/removes the delta.",
        "questionnaireAtom and the React context's `questionnaire` are two copies of the same data updated at different times: context updates during render, the atom only in a useEffect. Derived selectors (questionIdByLinkIdAtom, useVisibleTopLevelIndices, useHiddenQuestionIds) therefore lag the rendered tree by one paint on every re-seed. QuestionField reads its `question` from props (context path), not the atom.",
        "evaluateEnableWhen is a frozen behavior-exact port: unanswered dependency → false for every operator; comparisons run over ALL of the dependent question's values; normalizeValue (boolean→'Yes'/'No', number→String) applies unconditionally before every operator and also to literal-boolean condition answers in equals/not_equals. Do not 'fix' it.",
        "Visibility: QuestionField returns null when !enabled && disabled_display !== 'protected'; 'protected' questions still render but greyed via effectiveDisabled. useVisibleTopLevelIndices exists only so pagination never serves a blank page — a one-scroll canvas can drop it and rely on QuestionField's own null return.",
        "disabled resolution order: mode === 'readonly' || question.read_only === true, then OR'd with !enabled. Groups pass this down as a <fieldset disabled> so children are natively disabled too — a new group renderer that drops the fieldset must re-thread disabled explicitly.",
        "styling_metadata is untrusted author data: always route both `classes` and `containerClasses` through sanitizeStylingClasses. Contract per README: `classes` decorates the question's outer container, `containerClasses` lays out a group's sub-question container. Today QuestionField applies containerClasses (not classes) to a leaf question's wrapper, so a leaf's `classes` is silently never rendered — preserve or fix deliberately, but know a new module changing it alters deployed forms.",
        "Repeats: only non-choice, non-structured, non-display types with repeats===true render one input per entry. Positional writes must go through withEntryAt (gap-padding, never splice); single-entry mode (valueIndex undefined) must keep whole-array replace/clear semantics — text/number/time clear to values: [], boolean/date always write a 1-element array.",
        "The legacy structured prop bag is positional-by-name and untyped (ComponentType<any>): {question, questionnaireResponse, updateQuestionnaireResponseCB(values, questionId, note?), disabled, errors, clearError, index, withLabel, patientId, encounterId, facilityId}. Components also declare questionnaireId/questionnaireSlug (MedicationRequestQuestion, ServiceRequestQuestion) and organizations (EncounterQuestion) which the current slot does NOT pass — a fill-capable renderer should thread them. entry.requires gates rendering on subject keys.",
        "errorsAtom currently has readers but no writer and clearError is a no-op — this is the designated seam for the fill/submit path, which must add the writer, a real clearError and a 'fill' RendererMode. Error text renders as `error.msg ?? error.error` filtered by question_id.",
        "DOM id contract for a11y and Playwright: label id `question-label-${id}` (aria-labelledby target for chip groups), input id `question-input-${id}`, repeat entries `question-input-${id}-${i}` for i>0. Chip inputs (boolean, choice-with-options) must NOT be wrapped in the bordered box; bordered inputs pair with the merged NoteAffordance via rounded-r-none/border-r-0 on the control.",
        "There is no per-question wrapper/decoration seam today: depth===0 hardcodes TopLevelCard inside QuestionField/QuestionGroupCard, and group children are rendered by direct QuestionField recursion. A builder canvas needs an injected render-prop/context slot (e.g. renderQuestionShell({question, depth, children})) threaded through BOTH QuestionField and QuestionGroupCard, plus stable ids/refs per question for scroll-to-selection.",
        "The renderer's public surface is QuestionnaireRenderer + renderer/types only (store/context/registries are internal, no barrel file). Legacy src/components/Questionnaire imports are allowlisted in README (ValueSetSelect, SelectOrCreateValueset, data/StructuredFormData, QuestionTypes/* via structured/registry.tsx, OrgSelector) — a new module adding a legacy dependency must update that allowlist."
