ured questions) POST/PUT `/api/v1/form_submission/` and then **`navigate(...)` to the encounter updates page**.\n\n**Mount sites.** `QuestionnaireForm` is only mounted by `EncounterQuestionnaire` (src/components/Patient/EncounterQuestionnaire.tsx), which is wired in src/Routers/routes/ConsultationRoutes.tsx at 5 paths (`…/encounter/:encounterId/questionnaire[/:questionnaireId]`, `…/patient/:patientId/consultation`, `…/patient/:patientId/questionnaire`, `/patient/:patientId/questionnaire`). `onSubmit` navigates to `/updates`.\n\n**Mounting structured components elsewhere.** `STRUCTURED_REGISTRY` already declares the context each needs; `StructuredQuestionSlot` renders a dashed placeholder when `subject[key]` is missing. Providers actually required: QueryClientProvider (all), i18n, sonner `<Toaster/>` (App.tsx), and **AuthUserContext** — `useAuthUser()` *throws* and is called by MedicationRequestQuestion, ServiceRequestQuestion, AppointmentQuestion. **No react-hook-form anywhere** — zero `useForm`/`FormProvider`/`useFormContext` in QuestionTypes; state is plain `useState` + the update callback. PermissionContext is not used by any structured component (only `useCanWriteQuestionnaire`); `PermissionProvider` wraps everything in AppRouter.tsx:137 anyway. raviger location is read implicitly: `useQueryParams` in MedicationRequestQuestion (`?prescription`) and EncounterQuestion (`?toDischarge=true`), and `useFullPath` inside `useCurrentFacilitySilently`.\n\n**Biggest trap:** MedicationRequestQuestion **ignores the `facilityId` prop** and derives it from the URL via `useCurrentFacilitySilently()` (src/pages/Facility/utils/useCurrentFacility.tsx), as do ValueSetSearchContent and MedicationValueSetSelect. Under `/admin/questionnaires/:id/edit` facilityId is `undefined`, so facility-scoped valueset/medication/template lookups silently degrade; only the facility-settings builder route gets a real id. That hook also calls `useFullPath()` then throws *before* `useQuery`, so hook counts differ between facility and non-facility paths — navigating across that boundary without remount trips React.\n\n**Side effects a preview host must guard.** Allergy/Symptom/Diagnosis/MedicationStatement/MedicationRequest each fetch the patient's existing records on mount and immediately write them into the response via `updateQuestionnaireResponseCB`; the only escape hatch is the sentinel `patientId === \"preview\"` (`enabled: !isPreview`, `disableAPI={isPreview}` on HistoricalRecordSelector). EncounterQuestion has **no** preview guard: it GETs the encounter, honours `?toDischarge=true` by forcing status DISCHARGED, and mutates `period.end` in an effect. FileQuestion writes `[{type:\"files\", value: []}]` on mount and mounts camera/audio capture dialogs. ChargeItemQuestion's auto-add effect lists `updateQuestionnaireResponseCB` and `chargeItems` in its deps — the slot passes a fresh inline arrow each render, a real loop hazard. Add-to-template flows in MedicationRequest/ServiceRequest issue real POSTs and toasts. AppointmentQuestion uses the global `scheduleServiceTypeAtom`, which resolves against the renderer's private Jotai store (RendererContext), isolating it from the rest of the app. No structured component navigates.\n",
